[27.903816334,"o","● The app was down because the backend crashed, and it's now fixed. All\r\n  three services (backend, frontend, worker) are running and ready.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mCause:\u001b[0m at 19:05:12 someone ran \u001b[94mstackctl infra restart -s db\u001b[0m, which\r\n  restarted the database. The backend's Postgres pool got \u001b[94mterminating\r\n  connection due to administrator command\u001b[0m. It had no handler for that\r\n  error, so the process crashed. The dev script then sat on \"Waiting for\r\n  file changes before restarting…\", so the backend stayed \"running\" but\r\n  never came back. The frontend stayed not-ready because it depends on the\r\n  backend.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mFix:\u001b[0m I ran \u001b[94mstackctl service restart -s backend\u001b[0m. It came back healthy and\r\n  the frontend followed.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mFollow-up:\u001b[0m the backend will crash again on any future database restart\r\n  or dropped connection. The fix is an \u001b[94merror\u001b[0m listener on the pg Pool\r\n  (\u001b[94mpool.on('error', …)\u001b[0m) so a dropped idle connection doesn't throw as an\r\n  unhandled event. I haven't chang"]
[27.904019625,"o","ed any code. Do you want me to add that\r\n  handler?\r\n\r\n"]
